stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> START

    state "START (Initialize In-Memory State)" as START
    state "Node: intake" as intake
    state "Decision: _after_intake" as after_intake <<choice>>
    state "Node: extract_facts" as extract_facts
    state "Node: attribute_sources" as attribute_sources
    state "Node: detect_missing" as detect_missing
    state "Node: detect_contradictions" as detect_contradictions
    state "Node: associate_evidence" as associate_evidence
    state "Node: assess_jurisdiction" as assess_jurisdiction
    state "Node: validate_and_route" as validate_and_route
    state "Decision: _after_validation" as after_validation <<choice>>
    state "Node: human_review" as human_review
    state "Node: police_review" as police_review
    state "Node: build_report" as build_report
    state "END" as END

    START --> intake: Initial State (raw_input, trusted_events)
    
    note right of intake
        Reducer: keep_original
        Sets original_statement & SHA256 nonce.
        Raises ImmutableStatementError on modification.
        Validates statement length > 0.
    end note

    intake --> after_intake
    after_intake --> extract_facts: input_valid == True
    after_intake --> validate_and_route: input_valid == False (Empty Statement)

    extract_facts --> attribute_sources: Deterministic regex extractions + Grounded LLM items
    
    note right of attribute_sources
        Verifies exact character spans:
        T[start:end] == span_text
        Mismatched spans -> rejected_items
    end note

    attribute_sources --> detect_missing: Kept facts with valid spans
    detect_missing --> detect_contradictions: Evaluates core statutory gaps (datetime, location)
    detect_contradictions --> associate_evidence: Evaluates internal conflicts
    associate_evidence --> assess_jurisdiction: Links user attachments & verified police events
    assess_jurisdiction --> validate_and_route: Point-in-polygon containment & 100m buffer

    note right of validate_and_route
        Evaluates 8 Safety Gates:
        1. Statement input validity
        2. Statement SHA256 integrity
        3. All facts grounded with valid spans
        4. Zero contradiction conflicts
        5. Unambiguous inside jurisdiction (>100m)
        6. Zero missing core fields
        7. Zero high-risk unflagged patterns
        8. Zero node execution errors
    end note

    validate_and_route --> after_validation
    after_validation --> police_review: All 8 criteria satisfied (route == "ready_for_police_review")
    after_validation --> human_review: Any criteria failed (route == "human_review_required")

    note left of human_review
        Fail-safe fallback:
        Default route for all edge cases,
        near-boundary coordinates, or errors.
    end note

    human_review --> build_report: ReviewDecision payload
    police_review --> build_report: ReviewDecision payload

    build_report --> END: Emits structured draft, officer checklist, and audit log
